.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH split 1  "split " 
.SH NAME
split \- Construct and validate a real series of commits from the detected clusters, entirely inside a disposable temporary worktree. Never touches the current branch or checkout; nothing is merged, reset, or pushed. `\-\-apply`\-style automation onto the real branch is deliberately not implemented (Phase V territory)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsplit\fR [\fB\-\-staged\fR] [\fB\-\-discard\-worktree\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Construct and validate a real series of commits from the detected clusters, entirely inside a disposable temporary worktree. Never touches the current branch or checkout; nothing is merged, reset, or pushed. `\-\-apply`\-style automation onto the real branch is deliberately not implemented (Phase V territory)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-staged\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-discard\-worktree\fR
Remove the temporary worktree after presenting the plan. The branch it built (and its commits) are kept either way — this only controls whether the scratch working directory sticks around for inspection
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
